},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/PolicyResponse":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PolicyResponse"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PolicyResponse","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/policyresponse","title":"PolicyResponse","abstract":[{"code":"GET","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" response: the stored policy plus the unknown-AAGUID action it currently "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"resolves to"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"unknown_aaguid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is nullable, where "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" means “use this mode’s default” (deny under"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"direct_required","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", allow otherwise). A client that only saw the stored "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" would have to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"re-derive that rule itself to display what the policy actually does — and a security rule"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implemented twice is a security rule that will eventually disagree with itself. So the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"server resolves it once, here, and reports both: the admin’s stored intent and its effect."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PolicyResponse"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AttestationMode":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AttestationMode"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AttestationMode","title":"AttestationMode","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AttestationMode"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/attestationmode","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"What attestation conveyance a registration ceremony requests, and whether the policy is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"enforced at all. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"None"},{"text":" is the default and reproduces today’s behavior byte-for-byte:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"evaluate"},{"text":" allows every registration unconditionally, with no MDS lookup (D8 step 1).","type":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CertificationLevel":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CertificationLevel"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CertificationLevel","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/certificationlevel","title":"CertificationLevel","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"FIDO certification level, as recorded in an MDS "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"statusReports"},{"type":"text","text":" entry’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FIDO_CERTIFIED*"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"status. Variant order is significant: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"derive(PartialOrd, Ord)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"L1 < L1Plus < L2 < L2Plus < L3 < L3Plus"},{"type":"text","text":", which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WebauthnAttestationPolicy::evaluate"},{"type":"text","text":" (D8 step 9) relies on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directly for the "},{"code":"min_certification","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" boundary check ("},{"code":"entry_level >= policy_min","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CertificationLevel"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/PolicyResponse/init(allowedAaguids:blockRevokedStatus:blockedAaguids:minCertification:mode:requireFidoCertified:unknownAaguid:effectiveUnknownAaguid:)":{"